{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "The ruling house of Alethkar, whose colours are white and a deep \"Kholin blue\".",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "12" }]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "The King's Guard, soldiers sworn to protect Alethkar's king, are administered directly by Dalinar.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "18" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Like all Alethi princes, the Kholins descend from the Sunmaker Sadees. His ten sons were denied the throne, and their infighting created the princedoms; the Kholins come from one of those sons.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "24" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dalinar's crest shapes the glyphs khokh and linil into a tower and a crown, worn on his army's armour, clothing and banners. Elhokar's uses the same glyphs as a sword and crown.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "28" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Kholins hold a very large number of Shardblades between the family and its army, over thirty after the ten armies were united.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "5" }]
    }
  ],
  "history": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Unification",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "26" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "19" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "The Kholin family began expanding around 1139, when Gavilar and Dalinar led a conquest of the other highprinces, uniting Alethkar into one kingdom by 1148.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "26" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "A year into their war, the Kholins found allies in Toh and his sister Evi, who was betrothed into the family to seal the alliance.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "19" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Kings of Alethkar",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "22" },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "56" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "52" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "12" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "67" }
              ]
            },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "76" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Gavilar took the Alethi crown and married Navani; their children are Jasnah and Elhokar. Dalinar and his wife Evi had Adolin and Renarin.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "22" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Around 1155 Dalinar attacked Akak and claimed the island for Alethkar.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "56" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "52" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "After Gavilar's assassination Elhokar became king. The highprinces swore the Vengeance Pact, and Elhokar, Dalinar, Adolin and Renarin went to the Shattered Plains, moving the seat of power with them.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "12" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "67" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dalinar proposes a joint assault deep into the Shattered Plains to unite the highprinces; Aladar, Roion and Sebarial join him.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "76" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The True Desolation",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "12" }]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "With Urithiru and the Oathgates in reach, Dalinar founds the Coalition of Monarchs to resist the enemy, led with Navani and Jasnah.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "12" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
